Title: SIGNAL LOSS
Author: Jordan Ellis
Draft date: June 2026

FADE IN:


INT. ORBITAL RELAY STATION - COMMAND DECK - DAY

KARA VENN watches the array. A GOLD DATA CHIP sits in a labeled tray: KUIPER LOG — DO NOT ERASE.
KARA
Relay Seven, confirm packet integrity.
Static. One line resolves: ORIGIN UNKNOWN.

INT. LUNAR MISSION CONTROL - BRIEFING ROOM - DAY

NOLAN REED briefs LT. MARTINEZ and DR. SINGH.
NOLAN
Venn caught a ghost signal. We treat it as classified until verified.
SINGH
If that registry is correct, the Meridian went missing in 2014.

INT. ORBITAL RELAY STATION - SERVER BAY - NIGHT

Kara copies the burst onto the GOLD DATA CHIP. A secondary file unlocks — audio only.
KARA
That's not telemetry. That's a voice.

INT. CREW QUARTERS - ORBITAL STATION - NIGHT

Martinez packs a go-bag. Singh reviews medical supplies.
MARTINEZ
Reed wants a four-person team. We launch at 0600.

EXT. LUNAR TRANSIT DOCK - NIGHT

Nolan boards Aurora Six with a BLACK CASE. The shuttle seals.
NOLAN
No broadcast trail. We slip quiet.

INT. ORBITAL RELAY STATION - COMMAND DECK - DAY

Kara plays the audio — distorted, urgent: Reed, do not come alone. She freezes the waveform.
KARA
The voice matches Captain Hale. Meridian's last commander.

INT. AURORA SIX - COCKPIT - DAY

Nolan plots a course outward. Martinez straps in beside him.
MARTINEZ
Venn wants us to abort. She says the coordinates are a trap.
NOLAN
Then we walk in with our eyes open.

INT. ORBITAL RELAY STATION - COMM BOOTH - NIGHT

Kara opens a secure line. Singh's face appears on screen.
SINGH
I'm coming up to relay. If Hale is alive, he won't be human-shaped.

INT. DEEP-SPACE OBSERVATION NOOK - NIGHT

Through the viewport: a faint beacon pulses at the edge of scan range. Kara compares it to the chip data — a perfect match.
KARA
Nolan, the Meridian is out there. And it's still breathing.

INT. AURORA SIX - COCKPIT - NIGHT

The beacon grows on the forward display. Nolan grips the BLACK CASE, jaw set.
NOLAN
Aurora Six to Meridian. This is Nolan Reed. Respond.
Silence — then a single word crawls across comms: FINALLY.

FADE OUT.


THE END
